      "writtenOn": "2021-10-18T21:51:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The gpio_map.h defines the GPIO interrupt handler, like: \n  GPIO_INT(GPIO_USB_C0_BC12_INT_L, GPIO_INT_EDGE_FALLING, usb0_evt)\n\nThe `shim/src/gpio.c` driver registers a combined GPIO callback function to Zephyr. When the GPIO signal falls, it triggers the callback function and then call the individual handler, like the `usb0_evt()`.\n\nSince these interrupt handlers are removed from gpio_map.h, you need to register these GPIO callbacks to Zephyr, similar to what `shim/src/gpio.c` does.",
      "parentUuid": "0be77486_656f9254",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 47,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 47,
        "endChar": 38
      },
      "revId": "bbf259b35250132e1421f568e671f705a538b011",
